# runtime data — dsh reasoning-core territory
.dsh/
# ego trajectory index (memento) — runtime data, contains real conversations, not committed
.memento/
# local env config (copied from .env.example, not committed)
.env
# people/ is NOT ignored (2026-10-12): gitignore was never the privacy mechanism.
# The rule is upstream — private things (health, emotions, family specifics) are not
# written down anywhere at all, discussed and let go. Hiding the directory only hid
# the migratable part, and left the private part free to be written elsewhere.
#
# The one exception is narrow and named on purpose: an interview outline whose own
# frontmatter says privacy is his to present (health, family, fears). It stays local
# until he rules on what may be published.
people/*/INTERVIEW.md
.dolores.yml
